+Use case: precise-object-edit
+Edit target image1: our APPROVED ORIGINAL pixel-art Yakudza portrait reference board640x640, EXACT2columns2rows,320x320 cells. Each cell is an EXACT2x nearest presentation of a160x160 approved game portrait. Top row neutral expression duplicated; bottom row angry expression duplicated. This is our own previously approved artwork, not a photograph. Preserve exact identity, pixel positions, head/hair/face geometry, pose, black tee, thick fictional heavy body, phone, outlines, palette, framing and transparent silhouette. Do NOT redesign or beautify this recognizable character.
+Create ONLY these FOUR precise feature edits, same fixed grid and same registration:
+TOP LEFT: neutral TALK, change only lips/mouth into a modest visibly OPEN speaking mouth with small dark mouth interior, subtle teeth/tongue pixel accents, about8–11 native pixels high. Keep nose/cheeks/jaw/eyes/brows and head motionless. This is quiet speech, NOT an angry shout, catchphrase O-face or full expression change.
+TOP RIGHT: neutral BLINK, change ONLY both eye interiors/lids: both eyes fully CLOSED as narrow clear curved dark lid lines with appropriate skin ramps. Preserve the exact eyebrows and neutral calm face. No open pupils/sclera visible, not just looking down or squinting one eye.
+BOTTOM LEFT: angry TALK, ONLY mouth/lips modestly open speaking, same restrained small interior height as neutral talk, while angry brows/eyes/nose/face remain EXACTLY the approved angry base. No jaw stretch or head tilt.
+BOTTOM RIGHT: angry BLINK, ONLY both eyelids FULLY CLOSED; keep SAME furrowed angry eyebrows and all other facial geometry. No visible pupils or sclera, not just a harder squint.
+Keep every other pixel as close to original as possible. Critical registration: don't shift or scale any face, mouth or eyes; approved mouth center is near native(x99,y93), eye lines near native y67, nose base y80. Changed mouth region should stay native x84..112,y86..104; closed eyelids near native x65..88,y63..73 andx98..113,y61..72. These are reference-native coordinates within each160px portrait, multiply by2 for current320px cells. Do not add labels, text, panel borders or UI.
+TRUE deliberate low-resolution pixel art: unchanged hard square2x2pixel clusters, solid flat colors from original31-color palette, no antialiasing, gradients, blurry paint, photographic fragments or smooth skin. Transparent PNG background; no white matte, glow, painted checkerboard or new shadow. Final board same2x2 layout, all four busts remain the same exact size and eye-level as input.
